  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0350' contains 8 tables. The 'Ticket_Type' table represents the type of ticket, including its description, whether it includes a workshop, its name, and price. The 'Discount_Code' table represents a discount code, including its amount, name, and type. The 'Meeting' table represents a meeting, including its date, description, end time, name, room, and start time. The 'Workshop' table represents a workshop, including its capacity, date, description, end time, location, name, requirements, and start time. The 'Speaker' table represents a speaker, including their bio, company, and name. The 'Participant' table represents a participant, including their company, discount code ID, email, name, and ticket ID. The 'Meeting_Speaker' table represents the many-to-many relationship between meetings and speakers, with each row representing a meeting-speaker pair. The 'Workshop_Speaker' table represents the many-to-many relationship between workshops and speakers, with each row representing a workshop-speaker pair. All columns allow null values, and primary keys are used to enforce entity integrity. Foreign keys are used to enforce referential integrity, with CASCADE on delete and update rules.\n```python\n# This is a sample Python code to create the schema\nimport sqlite3\n# Connect to SQLite database\nconn = sqlite3.connect('rschema_0350.db')\nc = conn.cursor()\n# Create tables\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Ticket_Type(\nDescription VARCHAR(255),\nIncludes_Workshop VARCHAR(255),\nName VARCHAR(255),\nPrice FLOAT,\nTicket_ID INTEGER PRIMARY KEY\n)\n''')\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Discount_Code(\nAmount FLOAT,\nDiscount_Code_ID INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\nName VARCHAR(255),\nType VARCHAR(255)\n)\n''')\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Meeting(\nDate DATETIME,\nDescription VARCHAR(255),\nEnd_Time DATETIME,\nMeeting_ID INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\nName VARCHAR(255),\nRoom VARCHAR(255),\nStart_Time DATETIME\n)\n''')\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Workshop(\nCapacity INTEGER,\nDate DATETIME,\nDescription VARCHAR(255),\nEnd_Time DATETIME,\nLocation VARCHAR(255),\nName VARCHAR(255),\nRequirements VARCHAR(255),\nStart_Time DATETIME,\nWorkshop_ID INTEGER PRIMARY KEY\n)\n''')\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Speaker(\nBio VARCHAR(255),\nCompany VARCHAR(255),\nName VARCHAR(255),\nSpeaker_ID INTEGER PRIMARY KEY\n)\n''')\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Participant(\nCompany VARCHAR(255),\nDiscount_Code_ID INTEGER NOT NULL,\nEmail VARCHAR(255),\nName VARCHAR(255),\nParticipant_ID INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\nTicket_ID INTEGER NOT NULL,\nFOREIGN KEY(Discount_Code_ID) REFERENCES Discount_Code(Discount_Code_ID),\nFOREIGN KEY(Ticket_ID) REFERENCES Ticket_Type(Ticket_ID)\n)\n''')\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Meeting_Speaker(\nMeeting_ID INTEGER NOT NULL,\nSpeaker_ID INTEGER NOT NULL,\nPRIMARY KEY(Meeting_ID, Speaker_ID),\nFOREIGN KEY(Meeting_ID) REFERENCES Meeting(Meeting_ID),\nFOREIGN KEY(Speaker_ID) REFERENCES Speaker(Speaker_ID)\n)\n''')\nc.execute('''\nCREATE TABLE Workshop_Speaker(\nSpeaker_ID INTEGER NOT NULL,\nWorkshop_ID INTEGER NOT NULL,\nPRIMARY KEY(Workshop_ID, Speaker_ID),\nFOREIGN KEY(Speaker_ID) REFERENCES Speaker(Speaker_ID),\nFOREIGN KEY(Workshop_ID) REFERENCES Workshop(Workshop_ID)\n)\n''')\n# Commit the changes and close the connection\nconn.commit()\nconn.close()\n```",
  "gold_question": "The design of a technology conference management system is as follows:\nThe conference has participants, whose information includes Participant ID, Name, Company, and Email.\nThe conference offers various types of tickets, with ticket information including Ticket ID, Name, Description, Price, and whether it includes workshops, with each participant limited to purchasing one ticket.\nParticipants can use discount codes to purchase tickets, with discount code information including Code, Name, Type, and Amount.\nAfter purchasing tickets, participant ticket records are generated, containing Participant ID, Ticket ID, Discount Code ID, and Net Price.\nThe conference schedules multiple meetings, with meeting information including Name, Description, Date, Start Time, End Time, and Room.\nFurthermore, the conference also offers workshops, with workshop information including Name, Description, Requirements, Location, Date, Start Time, End Time, and Capacity.\nEach meeting or workshop can have multiple speakers, with speaker information including Name, Company, and Description.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0350.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0350\nCREATE TABLE `ticket_type` (\n  `ticket_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `includes_workshop` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ticket_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `discount_code` (\n  `discount_code_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`discount_code_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `meeting` (\n  `meeting_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `room` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meeting_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `workshop` (\n  `workshop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `capacity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `requirements` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`workshop_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `speaker` (\n  `speaker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `bio` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `company` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`speaker_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `participant` (\n  `participant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `discount_code_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ticket_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`participant_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `participant_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`discount_code_id`) REFERENCES `discount_code` (`discount_code_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `participant_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`ticket_id`) REFERENCES `ticket_type` (`ticket_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `meeting_speaker` (\n  `meeting_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `speaker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meeting_id`, `speaker_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `meeting_speaker_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`meeting_id`) REFERENCES `meeting` (`meeting_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `meeting_speaker_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`speaker_id`) REFERENCES `speaker` (`speaker_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `workshop_speaker` (\n  `workshop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `speaker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`workshop_id`, `speaker_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `workshop_speaker_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`workshop_id`) REFERENCES `workshop` (`workshop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `workshop_speaker_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`speaker_id`) REFERENCES `speaker` (`speaker_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
